## Why This Is Asked

Telemetry quality is critical for root cause analysis and cross-service tracing; this checks practical skills for CI, instrumentation, and rollback safety.

## Key Concepts

- Telemetry integrity, trace propagation, OpenTelemetry, CI gates, canary deployments
- Error budgets and dashboards alignment
- Synthetic validation and fallback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// OpenTelemetry middleware for trace propagation
const { trace, context, propagation } = require('@opentelemetry/api');

function ensureTraceId(req, res, next) {
  const carrier = propagation.createExtractHeadersCarrier(req.headers);
  const ctx = propagation.extract(context.active(), carrier);

  if (!trace.getSpan(ctx).spanContext().traceId) {
    const tracer = trace.getTracer('default');
    const span = tracer.startSpan('fallback-trace');
    propagation.inject(context.active(), carrier);
  }
  next();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure telemetry coverage and what would trigger a rollback?
- What trade-offs exist when dropping events missing trace_id?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to handle external dependency fragility, multi-tenant isolation, and production risk management. The question evaluates end-to-end instrumentation, resilience patterns, and practical operational procedures rather than theoretical knowledge.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end observability with OpenTelemetry
- Retry budgets with exponential backoff and jitter
- Circuit breakers with configurable thresholds and recovery
- Backpressure through token bucket rate limiting
- Idempotent retries with deduplication keys
- Progressive canary rollouts with automated rollback
- Incident runbooks and alerting thresholds
- SLO/SLI definition and percentile-based monitoring

## Code Example

```javascript
// Circuit breaker around identity provider
class CircuitBreaker {
  constructor(threshold = 5, timeout = 3000) {
    this.failureCount = 0;
    this.threshold = threshold;
    this.timeout = timeout;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
    this.lastFailure = null;
  }

  async execute(operation) {
    if (this.state === 'OPEN') {
      if (Date.now() - this.lastFailure > this.timeout) {
        this.state = 'HALF_OPEN';
      } else {
        throw new Error('Circuit breaker is OPEN');
      }
    }

    try {
      const result = await operation();
      this.onSuccess();
      return result;
    } catch (error) {
      this.onFailure();
      throw error;
    }
  }

  onSuccess() {
    this.failureCount = 0;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
  }

  onFailure() {
    this.failureCount++;
    this.lastFailure = Date.now();
    if (this.failureCount >= this.threshold) {
      this.state = 'OPEN';
    }
  }
}
```

Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a practical reliability strategy for multi-tenant, geo-distributed services under sudden load, balancing fairness and SLA adherence.

Key Concepts

- QoS with quotas and burst budgets
- Ingress-level enforcement and sidecar orchestration
- Dynamic rate limiting and circuit breakers
- Cross-region traffic steering and graceful degradation
- Observability: SLI/SLO dashboards, latency tails, queue depth
- Rollout/rollback: staged changes, synthetic tests, rapid revert

Code Example

```javascript
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(capacity, fillRate) {
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.fillRate = fillRate; // tokens per second
    this.last = Date.now();
  }
  allow(n = 1) {
    this._inject();
    if (this.tokens >= n) { this.tokens -= n; return true; }
    return false;
  }
  _inject() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.last) / 1000;
    this.last = now;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + elapsed * this.fillRate);
  }
}
```

Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure and trigger a regional SLA breach, and what would your kill-switch look like?
- What data would you surface in dashboards to operators during a flash spike?

## Why This Is Asked

